--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party component: ELSEPA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT License above covers the code written for this project (the web
application, the optional server, the WebAssembly build scripts, the tests and
the documentation). It does NOT cover ELSEPA.

ELSEPA 2021 (package "elsepa-2020": programs ELSCATA and ELSCATM, subroutine
package RADIAL, their subroutines and atomic data tables) is the work of
F. Salvat, A. Jablonski and C. J. Powell:

  F. Salvat, A. Jablonski, C. J. Powell, Comput. Phys. Commun. 261 (2021) 107704,
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2020.107704

  (Original method description: Comput. Phys. Commun. 165 (2005) 157-190,
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2004.09.006)

  RADIAL subroutine package:
  F. Salvat and J. M. Fernandez-Varea, Comput. Phys. Commun. 240 (2019) 165-177,
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2019.02.011

This repository contains the 2021 (Fortran 90) version of ELSEPA in fortran/,
its atomic data tables in data/, and a WebAssembly build of both in
public/elsepa/.

These files are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial
3.0 Unported License (CC BY-NC 3.0). See fortran/ELSEPA-LICENSE.txt for full
attribution and licence details. In accordance with the licence, use of ELSEPA
is permitted for non-commercial purposes with appropriate attribution to the
authors.

Notice: At the request of the ELSEPA authors, the earlier (2005) version of
ELSEPA is no longer distributed with this software.
